{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Path-history follow-up to the readiness comment: of the 262 absent old paths among the 43 available leaves, Git recognizes 229 as renames at >=50% similarity (mostly src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler -> src/rebar/reconciler and tests/*/rebar_reconciler -> tests/*/reconciler). The remaining 33 have no >=50% rename match in this comparison; that does not establish deletion of their behavior or prose. The earlier 28/43 figure describes stale ticket paths, not 28 irrecoverable leaves. Re-scope should map the 229 renamed paths and investigate the 33 unmatched paths, then refresh immutable bases and block inventories before grouping commits."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792719379512277788,"uuid":"f45bd362-adbf-47c8-9029-0121d92d36cf"}